{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/849682-2ed-experienced-characters","id":849682,"title":"[2ED] Experienced Characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-19T05:19:05-07:00","id":849682,"title":"[2ED] Experienced Characters","content":"I need numbers for Experienced Characters in <b>Werewolf</b> ( or any other <b>CoD</b> game ). Did quick search in my Werewolf 2ED corebook and could not find it. Is there a section I miss it? <br /> <br /> <b>I finally find them in Vampire 2ED - are those numbers more or less appropriate to Uratha development?</b><br /> <br /> <i>Around the block - 5 <br /> Rising star - 10 <br /> Ancilla - 15<br /> Rank elder - 25<br /> Mover and shaker - 35<br /> Urban Legend - 50<br /> Methuselah - 100</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T05:36:39-07:00","id":849684,"title":"","content":"They look pretty appropriate for Werewolf numbers since the XP prices are relatively the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T10:55:55-07:00","id":849797,"title":"","content":"Moreso, Uratha gain exponentially more XP than other splats by dint of the Sacred Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T11:02:54-07:00","id":849800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/849682-2ed-experienced-characters?p=849797#post849797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreso, Uratha gain exponentially more XP than other splats by dint of the Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts are pretty up there too thanks to Satiety Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T11:03:50-07:00","id":849802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/849682-2ed-experienced-characters?p=849797#post849797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreso, Uratha gain exponentially more XP than other splats by dint of the Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think considering Diablerie/(potentially) Blood Beats and the fact that Vampires get beats for risking detachment, that is a less objectively true statement than people seem to realize around these parts. And Beasts get a bunch for Satiety bullshit.<br /> <br /> That and the fact that Werewolf is only 1 of 3 splats (if you include Beast) to have a 2nd Edition book anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T11:14:41-07:00","id":849806,"title":"","content":"<i>My view of it is more like this:</i><br /> <br /> Freshly Changed - 0 experience points<br /> Still kicking - 5<br /> Rising stars - 10 experience points<br /> Established pack - 25 experience points<br /> Elders/Scarred veterans - 50 experience points<br /> Urban Legends/Lords of all they survey - 100 experience points<br /> <br /> I feel like werewolf society is a bit more strict on what it takes to be considered renowned or and Elder. And it's harder to live that long anyway with the violent types of lives they lead (though I guess vampires political wheeling and dealings leads to a lot of lives getting cut short)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T11:15:29-07:00","id":849807,"title":"","content":"Good point. Demons have persistent conditions based on their Agenda, as well. And Mages have something comparable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T11:21:50-07:00","id":849808,"title":"","content":"I dunno how much of an easy time Beasts have regaining saciety at the same time they burn it. Uratha using Sacred Hunt plus Song in Your Heart basically get 3 beats on rolls of 3 successes or more. (1 from the exceptional success, 1 from resolving Persistent Inspired, then another from the exceptional success given condition.)<br /> <br /> For the whole pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T04:44:38-07:00","id":850494,"title":"","content":"Exceptional success does not give a beat by default. It gives a condition, either positive to you or negative to your enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T07:11:00-07:00","id":850530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/849682-2ed-experienced-characters?p=849808#post849808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno how much of an easy time Beasts have regaining saciety at the same time they burn it. Uratha using Sacred Hunt plus Song in Your Heart basically get 3 beats on rolls of 3 successes or more. (1 from the exceptional success, 1 from resolving Persistent Inspired, then another from the exceptional success given condition.)<br /> <br /> For the whole pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very specific scenario. Not uncommon, since I think most players understandably tend to try to drum up as many beats as they can, but there are a half dozen scenarios where one gets 2 beats in a turn, and being a werewolf on Siskur-Dah is not a requirement for most of them.<br /> <br /> It is only two beats, by the way. Most (if not all) of the Conditions you can get from an exceptional Success (Inspired, Invisible Predator, Symbolic Focus, etc.) don't grant a beat on resolution, as they don't offer opportunities for inconveniencing yourself in roleplay. They're strictly positive and are their own reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T07:23:26-07:00","id":850533,"title":"","content":"Resolving any condition grants beats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T07:40:33-07:00","id":850541,"title":"","content":"Didn't know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T07:47:36-07:00","id":850549,"title":"","content":"The exception are conditions that last longer and offer extra complications, like Ban.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}